WEBVTT

NOTE
Sample caption track for the mantine-audio documentation.

This is illustrative, not a transcript of the recording: it exists to show that cue text appears,
changes and clears while the audio plays. Cue times stay inside the clip's real duration (43.1s).

The `captions` kind is used because these lines describe sound rather than translate speech — that
is the distinction between `captions` and `subtitles`.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.000
[music starts]

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Captions on an audio player are rendered by
Audio.Captions — the browser draws nothing.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
An audio element has no picture,
so there is no surface to paint cues on.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The cue text is read from the TextTrack API
and rendered as ordinary DOM.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Use the CC button in the control bar
to switch these lines off and on.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Overlapping cues are shown on separate lines,
in the order they appear in the file.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
♪

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Like this second line, active at the same moment.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.500
[music fades]
